menu "Bluetooth Fast Pair"

choice BT_FAST_PAIR_PROVISION_SOURCE
	prompt "Fast Pair provisioning pipeline"
	default BT_FAST_PAIR_PROVISION_PARTITION
	help
	  Select how Fast Pair credentials (Model ID and Anti-Spoofing private key)
	  are placed on the device during the build and provisioning flow.

	  This is a sysbuild-level choice. It controls the build pipeline and which
	  application Kconfig options are forwarded to the default image via
	  sysbuild. It does not replace the corresponding choice in the application
	  Fast Pair Kconfig tree.

	config BT_FAST_PAIR_PROVISION_PARTITION
		bool "Flash partition (build-time hex merge)"
		help
		  Generate a Fast Pair provisioning hex file at build time and merge it
		  into the bt_fast_pair flash partition in the final image.

		  Use this on targets that define a bt_fast_pair partition (Partition
		  Manager or devicetree). Sysbuild generates the hex when Model ID and
		  Anti-Spoofing key are set (see SB_CONFIG_BT_FAST_PAIR_PROV_DATA).

		  Typical for single-image builds on nRF52/nRF53/nRF54 without TF-M /ns.
		  Not used on /ns (TF-M) secure-storage flows.

	config BT_FAST_PAIR_PROVISION_SECURE_STORAGE
		bool "KMU and Internal Trusted Storage (runtime provisioner)"
		help
		  Store credentials in hardware-protected storage instead of a flash
		  partition:
		  	- Anti-Spoofing private key in a CRACEN KMU slot
		  	(SB_CONFIG_BT_FAST_PAIR_ANTI_SPOOFING_PRIVATE_KEY_KMU_SLOT)
		  	- Model ID in PSA Internal Trusted Storage
		  	(SB_CONFIG_BT_FAST_PAIR_MODEL_ID_ITS_ID)

		  Requires a runtime provisioner image
		  (SB_CONFIG_BT_FAST_PAIR_RUNTIME_PROVISIONER) to write credentials
		  before the main application runs. The main application then reads
		  from KMU/ITS at runtime.

		  Intended for non-secure (TF-M) builds. Slot and ITS UID values must
		  match on provisioner and application images; sysbuild forwards them
		  to both via the Kconfig bridge.

endchoice

config BT_FAST_PAIR_RUNTIME_PROVISIONER
	bool "Build runtime provisioner image"
	default n
	depends on BT_FAST_PAIR_PROVISION_SECURE_STORAGE
	help
	  Build a provisioner application image that writes Fast Pair credentials
	  into KMU and Internal Trusted Storage at first boot (or when flashed).  
	  Enable together with BT_FAST_PAIR_PROVISION_SECURE_STORAGE. Use a
	  provisioner FILE_SUFFIX (for example mcuboot_provisioner or
	  provisioner) so sysbuild builds the writer image before the main app.

	  The provisioner registers SB_CONFIG_BT_FAST_PAIR_MODEL_ID and
	  SB_CONFIG_BT_FAST_PAIR_ANTI_SPOOFING_PRIVATE_KEY using the KMU slot and
	  ITS UID configured in this menu. Flash the provisioner image first
	  (preferably with --erase/--recover flag to clear old data), then the
	  main Fast Pair application.

config BT_FAST_PAIR_MODEL_ID
	hex "Set the Model ID used for Fast Pair provisioning"
	range 0x000000 0x1000000
	default 0x1000000
	help
	  Set the Model ID that is used to generate the Fast Pair provisioning data hex file.
	  The Model ID is obtained during device model registration in the Google Nearby Console.
	  Note that the corresponding SB_CONFIG_BT_FAST_PAIR_ANTI_SPOOFING_PRIVATE_KEY Kconfig
	  option must be supplied to trigger the generation of the Fast Pair provisioning data hex
	  file. The generation is indicated by the SB_CONFIG_BT_FAST_PAIR_PROV_DATA Kconfig.

	  The Model ID should be a value from the 0x000000 - 0xFFFFFF range. The additional
	  default value (0x1000000) that is outside of the actual range is only used to mark
	  this option as unset by the user.

config BT_FAST_PAIR_ANTI_SPOOFING_PRIVATE_KEY
	string "Set the Anti-Spoofing Private Key used for Fast Pair provisioning"
	help
	  Set the Anti-Spoofing Private Key that is used to generate the Fast Pair provisioning
	  data hex file. The Anti-Spoofing Private Key is obtained during device model registration
	  in the Google Nearby Console. Note that the corresponding SB_CONFIG_BT_FAST_PAIR_MODEL_ID
	  Kconfig option must be supplied to trigger the generation of the Fast Pair provisioning
	  data hex file The generation is indicated by the SB_CONFIG_BT_FAST_PAIR_PROV_DATA
	  Kconfig.

	  The Anti-Spoofing Private Key is confidential and must be handled securely. It is
	  recommended to store this key securely outside the code repository and pass it to
	  the project as an additional argument for the build command
	  (``-DSB_CONFIG_BT_FAST_PAIR_ANTI_SPOOFING_PRIVATE_KEY=<value>``).

config BT_FAST_PAIR_ANTI_SPOOFING_PRIVATE_KEY_KMU_SLOT
	int "CRACEN KMU slot for the Anti-Spoofing private key"
	default 30
	help
	  KMU slot index (RAW usage scheme) for the Anti-Spoofing Private Key
	  when BT_FAST_PAIR_PROVISION_SECURE_STORAGE is selected. The runtime provisioner
	  image imports the key from SB_CONFIG_BT_FAST_PAIR_ANTI_SPOOFING_PRIVATE_KEY
	  into this slot; the main Fast Pair application reads it from KMU at
	  runtime instead of the bt_fast_pair flash partition. Must match on
	  provisioner and application images (sysbuild forwards this value to both).

config BT_FAST_PAIR_MODEL_ID_ITS_ID
	int "PSA Internal Trusted Storage UID for the Model ID"
	default 2000
	help
	  PSA ITS uid for the 24-bit Model ID when BT_FAST_PAIR_PROVISION_SECURE_STORAGE is
	  selected. The runtime provisioner image writes SB_CONFIG_BT_FAST_PAIR_MODEL_ID
	  here; the main Fast Pair application reads it from ITS at runtime instead
	  of the bt_fast_pair flash partition. Must match on provisioner and
	  application images (sysbuild forwards this value to both).


config BT_FAST_PAIR_PROV_DATA
	bool
	depends on BT_FAST_PAIR_PROVISION_PARTITION
	depends on BT_FAST_PAIR_MODEL_ID != 0x1000000
	depends on BT_FAST_PAIR_ANTI_SPOOFING_PRIVATE_KEY != ""
	default y
	help
	  This option is automatically enabled when partition-based provisioning
	  (SB_CONFIG_BT_FAST_PAIR_PROVISION_PARTITION) is selected and both the Model ID
	  (SB_CONFIG_BT_FAST_PAIR_MODEL_ID) and the Anti-Spoofing Private Key
	  (SB_CONFIG_BT_FAST_PAIR_ANTI_SPOOFING_PRIVATE_KEY) are set.

	  When this option is enabled, sysbuild generates the Fast Pair provisioning data hex file
	  and merges it with the final output hex file that is uploaded on the chosen board target.

	  For the generation step to work correctly, the user must manually define the Fast Pair
	  partition. In the case of platforms that use the DTS for memory map description (for
	  example, nRF54H), the Fast Pair partition must be defined as a DTS node. In the case of
	  platforms that use the Partition Manager (PM) for memory map description (for example,
	  nRF54L), the Fast Pair partition must be a statically defined PM partition. The PM
	  solution also supports the dynamic generation of the partition definition if the
	  CONFIG_BT_FAST_PAIR Kconfig is enabled in the main (default) image. This is the only case
	  when the partition does not have to be manually defined by the user. Detailed
	  documentation regarding the Fast Pair partition definition can be found in the Fast Pair
	  integration guide.
endmenu
